PiBotPal licensing
=================

Current PiBotPal application, hardware transport, motion/geometry, Testing tab,
web UI, MCP/LLM integration, native clients, tests and documentation are MIT
licensed; see LICENSE. Copyright (c) 2026 Chris DiBona.

The direct Robot HAT implementation uses hardware register/wiring facts and
python-periphery (MIT), without importing SunFounder picrawler/robot_hat code.
The motion planner and teaching exercises are new implementations. SunFounder's
original GPLv3 programs remain separate and unchanged in ~/picrawler; see
references/README.md. Prior PiBotPal versions in Git history retain their
original notices; LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt is retained for historical reference.
No upstream GPL code is being relicensed.

Three.js 0.170.0 and OrbitControls retain the MIT license and attribution in
pibotpal/static/vendor/THREE-LICENSE.txt.

Runtime dependencies retain their own licenses. In particular the system
